---
import Icon from '@/components/Icon.astro';
import FilterScript from '@/components/FilterScript.astro';
---

<div class="tip mb-[10px]">
  <Icon name="graduation-cap" />
  <strong>What's a port?</strong> If an IP address is a building's street address, a <em
    >port number</em
  > is the apartment number inside. Port 80 = web, port 443 = secure web, port 22 = SSH remote access.
  Every service runs on a specific port.
</div><div class="table-filter">
  <input
    class="form-input"
    id="port-filter"
    placeholder="Search by port number, name, or protocol..."
    data-filter="#port-table tbody tr"
    type="search"
    autocomplete="off"
  />
</div><div class="table-wrap" id="port-table-wrap">
  <table class="ref-table" id="port-table">
    <thead><tr><th>Port</th><th>Service</th><th>Transport</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead
    ><tbody
      ><tr
        ><td class="mono">20</td><td><strong>FTP Data</strong></td><td>TCP</td><td
          >File transfer data channel</td
        ></tr
      ><tr
        ><td class="mono">21</td><td><strong>FTP Control</strong></td><td>TCP</td><td
          >File transfer commands</td
        ></tr
      ><tr
        ><td class="mono">22</td><td><strong>SSH</strong></td><td>TCP</td><td
          >Secure Shell encrypted remote access</td
        ></tr
      ><tr
        ><td class="mono">23</td><td><strong>Telnet</strong></td><td>TCP</td><td
          >Unencrypted remote access (legacy)</td
        ></tr
      ><tr
        ><td class="mono">25</td><td><strong>SMTP</strong></td><td>TCP</td><td
          >Simple Mail Transfer Protocol</td
        ></tr
      ><tr
        ><td class="mono">49</td><td><strong>TACACS+</strong></td><td>TCP</td><td
          >AAA authentication (Cisco)</td
        ></tr
      ><tr
        ><td class="mono">53</td><td><strong>DNS</strong></td><td>TCP/UDP</td><td
